Indus Insurance's monthly salary bill for its sales staff is PKR 3.6 million. Sales have fallen. The managing director is choosing between:
Option 1 – a bonus of 5% of the salary bill, paid every month if the sales target is met;
Option 2 – a training and promotion programme costing PKR 900,000 in its first year, with clear career steps for staff.

CareWell Hospitals has 1,500 staff in three hospitals in Lahore. Staff complain that they do not hear about changes to policies. Managers are choosing one method:
Option 1 – a printed monthly newsletter costing PKR 60 per copy, one copy per staff member each month;
Option 2 – a staff intranet and phone app: set-up cost PKR 800,000 plus PKR 150,000 per year maintenance;
Option 3 – a 30-minute weekly team meeting on each ward, led by ward managers.

Comfort Home Furniture sells sofas and beds in Karachi. Because of a recession, it expects sales to fall. Last year it sold 2,000 items at an average price of PKR 50,000. Managers are considering two options:
Option 1 – cut prices by 10%; they forecast this would lead to sales of 2,150 items;
Option 2 – keep prices the same and make 8 of its 40 staff redundant. Each of these staff costs PKR 60,000 per month.
